JSX allows us to write HTML-like code inside JavaScript.

Example:

function App() {
  const name = "Jaya";

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Hello {name}</h1>
      <p>Welcome to my React application.</p>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
Output:
Hello Jaya
Welcome to my React application.

You can use JavaScript expressions inside { }.

Example:

<h1>{10 + 20}</h1>

Output:

30